  "result": "Perfect! All 104 tests pass. I've successfully added VAT calculations to the invoice system:\n\n**Implementation:**\n\n1. **`lineVat()` function** in `src/invoices.js`:\n   - Calculates VAT for a single line after discount\n   - Formula: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) * vatRate / 100`\n   - Uses `roundCents()` for per-line rounding\n\n2. **Updated `invoiceTotals()`**:\n   - Returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - `subtotal` = sum of line totals\n   - `discount` = sum of line discounts\n   - `vat` = sum of per-line VAT amounts (important: VAT is rounded per line, not as a percentage of invoice total)\n   - `total` = subtotal - discount + vat\n\n3. **Updated `renderInvoiceText()`**:\n   - Shows `VAT:` line only when VAT > 0, displayed just above the total\n   - Uses `formatEuros()` for proper formatting\n\n4. **Comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - VAT calculation with different rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n   - VAT with discounts applied before VAT\n   - Per-line rounding verification\n   - Mixed VAT rates on single invoice\n   - Rendering with and without VAT\n\nThe system correctly implements VAT as a per-line calculation with per-line rounding, never as a percentage of the invoice total. \u2714",
